INT. SALVAGE TUG "HALCYON" - COMMAND DECK - SHIP TIME 0412

Dim blue. Instrument glow. Frost on the edge of a viewport that shows nothing but black and a distant, tumbling hull.

COMMANDER ISSA (40s, grey jumpsuit, scar through one eyebrow) sits in the captain's chair, eyes on a scrolling console. ROOK (30s, engineer, pushed-up sleeves, grease on her cheek) kneels under an open panel, wiring. ENSIGN TARQUIN (20s, pressed uniform, nervous hands) stands at the comms station with a headset.

ISSA
Status on the derelict.

TARQUIN
Thermal reading's ambient, Commander. No heat signature.

ISSA
Life signs?

TARQUIN
None.

ROOK
(from under the panel)
Which means there's nothing to find, so why are we still here?

ISSA
Because it's salvage, Rook. Salvage pays.

ROOK
It pays if the thing doesn't kill us.

TARQUIN
(to the room)
Does anyone else feel that temperature drop?

Nobody answers. Issa taps the console. A pulse of green runs through the hull.

ISSA
Rook, how long until we're docked?

ROOK
Ninety minutes if I finish the seal.

ISSA
Do it in sixty.

ROOK
(muttering)
Sure. And I'll grow another arm.

She slides out, seals the panel, and wipes her hands. The deck lights flicker. A tone chimes.

TARQUIN
Commander, we have an incoming hail. From the derelict.

ISSA
Impossible.

TARQUIN
Audio only.

ISSA
Put it up.

A hiss of static. Then a thin voice, a whisper through a thousand miles of vacuum.

JONAH (V.O.)
(distorted, recorded)
...please... anyone... the hull is breached... we are still aboard...

TARQUIN
It's repeating. Same thirty seconds. Loop.

ROOK
Who's aboard? The manifest said the crew was evacuated.

ISSA
The manifest said a lot of things.

He stands. Straightens his jumpsuit. Looks at each of them in turn.

ISSA (CONT'D)
Rook, suit up. Tarquin, keep the channel open. I'm going over.

TARQUIN
Alone, Commander?

ISSA
Nobody else is qualified to be wrong.

ROOK
Sir, with respect, that's the stupidest thing I've ever heard.

ISSA
It's also the plan.

Rook sighs, grabs a helmet. Tarquin tightens his headset. At the airlock, the inner door cycles open with a soft pneumatic breath.

A figure stands inside, in a salvage suit that doesn't fit the Halcyon's fleet. JONAH (40s, a ragged beard behind a cracked faceplate, one glove missing) holds a flare gun in his remaining hand.

JONAH
Don't. Don't touch the console.

ISSA
Who are you?

JONAH
Jonah Reyes. Navigator, Mercator. I've been on that hull for fourteen months.

TARQUIN
(whisper)
That's impossible.

JONAH
It's the only thing I've been telling myself.

ROOK
(to herself, low)
Fourteen months.

Jonah steps forward, the flare gun trembling.

JONAH (CONT'D)
Commander. Listen to me. That loop isn't mine. I stopped sending it a year ago. Something else is using my voice.

Issa's hand finds the emergency stud on his chair arm. The lights go red. A claxon begins.

ISSA
Everyone to stations. Rook, seal the airlock. Tarquin, sever the hull link.

TARQUIN
Sever?

ISSA
Do it now!

Tarquin slams the break lever. The viewport flares. On the derelict, a long, slow light switches on, bright as a second sun, and turns toward the Halcyon.

JONAH
(quiet)
Too late.

The whole ship shudders. The flare gun drops from Jonah's hand and bounces on the deck, spinning, lighting every face in turn.
